EnquiryForm lays out a proposal or service request: TextFields in two columns, choices, a message box and one submit button.

- Markup: `<form class="aq-form" novalidate>` holding `aq-field` blocks (see TextField). Fields that need the full width (message, checkbox groups) add `aq-form__full`. End with `<div class="aq-form__actions">` holding one `aq-btn--primary` and a `<span class="aq-small" role="status">` for the result message.
- Select: `<select class="aq-field__input">`. Message: `<textarea class="aq-field__input">`.
- Checkbox group: `<fieldset class="aq-fieldset aq-field aq-form__full">` with a `<legend class="aq-field__label">` and `<div class="aq-checks">` of `<label><input type="checkbox"> System type</label>`.
- Mark optional fields, not required ones: `<span class="aq-field__optional">(optional)</span>` inside the label.
- Ask what an engineer can answer: project stage, system type, required capacity in L/h, standards, timeline. Capacity and temperature use the unit suffix.
- The submit label says what happens: "Request a proposal", "Send service request". The consumer provides validation and submission.
- Radio group (one answer): the checkbox-group markup with `type="radio"` and a shared `name`.
- File upload: `<input class="aq-field__file" type="file" multiple>` in a full-width `aq-field`, always optional, with help text naming the formats and saying files can be sent later.
- Conditional field: add `data-when="<option label>"` and `hidden`; the site shows it only while that option is ticked (for example pure steam capacity when "Pure steam generator" is chosen).
- Several triggers: separate option labels with `|` (`data-when="Sizing and budget proposal|Route assessment"`); the field shows while any of them is ticked. A tick inside a hidden conditional field does not count, so a follow-up question hides with its parent (for example an intent radio at the top of the form that reveals a sub-choice, which in turn reveals its own fields). Never use a label that repeats across groups, such as "Not sure yet", as a trigger.
- Pre-set from the linking page: a button that routes to a page with a form can carry `data-intent="<option label>|<option label>"` (in page content: hero `primary_cta_intent`, closing `cta.intent`). On arrival the form ticks those options and opens the conditional fields they trigger, with the same cascade rule, so a visitor from the feedwater page lands on "Feedwater review" with its questions showing. Every label must be an option of a radio or checkbox group on the target form (`python tools/design_system.py check` flags any that are not). The visitor can still change the choice.
- Steps, for long intake forms: `<form class="aq-form aq-form--steps">` with `<ol class="aq-form__progress">` (one `<li>` per step, `aria-current="step"` on the active one) and one `<fieldset class="aq-form__step" data-step="0">` per step, its `<legend class="aq-h3">` reading "Step 1 of 3: System scope". Inactive steps carry `hidden`. Each step ends in an `aq-form__actions` with Back (`aq-btn--secondary`) and Continue buttons (`data-step-go="<index>"`); only the last has the submit. Ask the technical questions first and contact details last; three steps at most.
